    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.accounts.tokens.create(account_id: string, name: string, policies: { id: string; effect: 'allow' | 'deny'; permission_groups: object[]; resources: object | object; }[], condition?: { request_ip?: { in?: token_condition_cidr_list[]; not_in?: token_condition_cidr_list[]; }; }, expires_on?: string, not_before?: string): { id?: string; condition?: object; expires_on?: string; issued_on?: string; last_used_on?: string; modified_on?: string; name?: string; not_before?: string; policies?: token_policy[]; status?: 'active' | 'disabled' | 'expired'; value?: token_value; }`\n\n**post** `/accounts/{account_id}/tokens`\n\nCreate a new Account Owned API token.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `account_id: string`\n  Account identifier tag.\n\n- `name: string`\n  Token name.\n\n- `policies: { id: string; effect: 'allow' | 'deny'; permission_groups: { id: string; meta?: { key?: string; value?: string; }; name?: string; }[]; resources: object | object; }[]`\n  List of access policies assigned to the token.\n\n- `condition?: { request_ip?: { in?: string[]; not_in?: string[]; }; }`\n  - `request_ip?: { in?: string[]; not_in?: string[]; }`\n    Client IP restrictions.\n\n- `expires_on?: string`\n  The expiration time on or after which the JWT MUST NOT be accepted for processing.\n\n- `not_before?: string`\n  The time before which the token MUST NOT be accepted for processing.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id?: string; condition?: { request_ip?: { in?: token_condition_cidr_list[]; not_in?: token_condition_cidr_list[]; }; }; expires_on?: string; issued_on?: string; last_used_on?: string; modified_on?: string; name?: string; not_before?: string; policies?: { id: string; effect: 'allow' | 'deny'; permission_groups: object[]; resources: object | object; }[]; status?: 'active' | 'disabled' | 'expired'; value?: string; }`\n\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `condition?: { request_ip?: { in?: string[]; not_in?: string[]; }; }`\n  - `expires_on?: string`\n  - `issued_on?: string`\n  - `last_used_on?: string`\n  - `modified_on?: string`\n  - `name?: string`\n  - `not_before?: string`\n  - `policies?: { id: string; effect: 'allow' | 'deny'; permission_groups: { id: string; meta?: { key?: string; value?: string; }; name?: string; }[]; resources: object | object; }[]`\n  - `status?: 'active' | 'disabled' | 'expired'`\n  - `value?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Cloudflare from 'cloudflare';\n\nconst client = new Cloudflare();\n\nconst token = await client.accounts.tokens.create({\n  account_id: '023e105f4ecef8ad9ca31a8372d0c353',\n  name: 'readonly token',\n  policies: [{\n  effect: 'allow',\n  permission_groups: [{ id: 'c8fed203ed3043cba015a93ad1616f1f' }, { id: '82e64a83756745bbbb1c9c2701bf816b' }],\n  resources: { foo: 'string' },\n}],\n});\n\nconsole.log(token);\n```",
