    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.user.auditLogs.list(id?: string, action?: { type?: string; }, actor?: { email?: string; ip?: string; }, before?: string | string, direction?: 'desc' | 'asc', export?: boolean, hide_user_logs?: boolean, page?: number, per_page?: number, since?: string | string, zone?: { name?: string; }): { id?: string; action?: object; actor?: object; interface?: string; metadata?: object; newValue?: string; oldValue?: string; owner?: object; resource?: object; when?: string; }`\n\n**get** `/user/audit_logs`\n\nGets a list of audit logs for a user account. Can be filtered by who made the change, on which zone, and the timeframe of the change.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `id?: string`\n  Finds a specific log by its ID.\n\n- `action?: { type?: string; }`\n  - `type?: string`\n    Filters by the action type.\n\n- `actor?: { email?: string; ip?: string; }`\n  - `email?: string`\n    Filters by the email address of the actor that made the change.\n  - `ip?: string`\n    Filters by the IP address of the request that made the change by specific IP address or valid CIDR Range.\n\n- `before?: string | string`\n  Limits the returned results to logs older than the specified date. A `full-date` that conforms to RFC3339.\n\n- `direction?: 'desc' | 'asc'`\n  Changes the direction of the chronological sorting.\n\n- `export?: boolean`\n  Indicates that this request is an export of logs in CSV format.\n\n- `hide_user_logs?: boolean`\n  Indicates whether or not to hide user level audit logs.\n\n- `page?: number`\n  Defines which page of results to return.\n\n- `per_page?: number`\n  Sets the number of results to return per page.\n\n- `since?: string | string`\n  Limits the returned results to logs newer than the specified date. A `full-date` that conforms to RFC3339.\n\n- `zone?: { name?: string; }`\n  - `name?: string`\n    Filters by the name of the zone associated to the change.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id?: string; action?: { result?: boolean; type?: string; }; actor?: { id?: string; email?: string; ip?: string; type?: 'user' | 'admin' | 'Cloudflare'; }; interface?: string; metadata?: object; newValue?: string; oldValue?: string; owner?: { id?: string; }; resource?: { id?: string; type?: string; }; when?: string; }`\n\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `action?: { result?: boolean; type?: string; }`\n  - `actor?: { id?: string; email?: string; ip?: string; type?: 'user' | 'admin' | 'Cloudflare'; }`\n  - `interface?: string`\n  - `metadata?: object`\n  - `newValue?: string`\n  - `oldValue?: string`\n  - `owner?: { id?: string; }`\n  - `resource?: { id?: string; type?: string; }`\n  - `when?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Cloudflare from 'cloudflare';\n\nconst client = new Cloudflare();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const auditLog of client.user.auditLogs.list()) {\n  console.log(auditLog);\n}\n```",
