      "## create\n\n`client.ssl.analyze.create(zone_id: string, bundle_method?: 'ubiquitous' | 'optimal' | 'force', certificate?: string): object`\n\n**post** `/zones/{zone_id}/ssl/analyze`\n\nReturns the set of hostnames, the signature algorithm, and the expiration date of the certificate.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `zone_id: string`\n  Identifier.\n\n- `bundle_method?: 'ubiquitous' | 'optimal' | 'force'`\n  A ubiquitous bundle has the highest probability of being verified everywhere, even by clients using outdated or unusual trust stores. An optimal bundle uses the shortest chain and newest intermediates. And the force bundle verifies the chain, but does not otherwise modify it.\n\n- `certificate?: string`\n  The zone's SSL certificate or certificate and the intermediate(s).\n\n### Returns\n\n- `object`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Cloudflare from 'cloudflare';\n\nconst client = new Cloudflare();\n\nconst analyze = await client.ssl.analyze.create({ zone_id: '023e105f4ecef8ad9ca31a8372d0c353' });\n\nconsole.log(analyze);\n```",
