      "## update\n\n`client.customCertificates.prioritize.update(zone_id: string, certificates: { id?: string; priority?: number; }[]): { id: string; zone_id: string; bundle_method?: bundle_method; custom_csr_id?: string; expires_on?: string; geo_restrictions?: geo_restrictions; hosts?: string[]; issuer?: string; keyless_server?: keyless_certificate; modified_on?: string; policy_restrictions?: string; priority?: number; signature?: string; status?: 'active' | 'expired' | 'deleted' | 'pending' | 'initializing'; uploaded_on?: string; }`\n\n**put** `/zones/{zone_id}/custom_certificates/prioritize`\n\nIf a zone has multiple SSL certificates, you can set the order in which they should be used during a request. The higher priority will break ties across overlapping 'legacy_custom' certificates.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `zone_id: string`\n  Identifier.\n\n- `certificates: { id?: string; priority?: number; }[]`\n  Array of ordered certificates.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; zone_id: string; bundle_method?: 'ubiquitous' | 'optimal' | 'force'; custom_csr_id?: string; expires_on?: string; geo_restrictions?: { label?: 'us' | 'eu' | 'highest_security'; }; hosts?: string[]; issuer?: string; keyless_server?: { id: string; created_on: string; enabled: boolean; host: string; modified_on: string; name: string; permissions: string[]; port: number; status: 'active' | 'deleted'; tunnel?: tunnel; }; modified_on?: string; policy_restrictions?: string; priority?: number; signature?: string; status?: 'active' | 'expired' | 'deleted' | 'pending' | 'initializing'; uploaded_on?: string; }`\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `zone_id: string`\n  - `bundle_method?: 'ubiquitous' | 'optimal' | 'force'`\n  - `custom_csr_id?: string`\n  - `expires_on?: string`\n  - `geo_restrictions?: { label?: 'us' | 'eu' | 'highest_security'; }`\n  - `hosts?: string[]`\n  - `issuer?: string`\n  - `keyless_server?: { id: string; created_on: string; enabled: boolean; host: string; modified_on: string; name: string; permissions: string[]; port: number; status: 'active' | 'deleted'; tunnel?: { private_ip: string; vnet_id: string; }; }`\n  - `modified_on?: string`\n  - `policy_restrictions?: string`\n  - `priority?: number`\n  - `signature?: string`\n  - `status?: 'active' | 'expired' | 'deleted' | 'pending' | 'initializing'`\n  - `uploaded_on?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Cloudflare from 'cloudflare';\n\nconst client = new Cloudflare();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const customCertificate of client.customCertificates.prioritize.update({ zone_id: '023e105f4ecef8ad9ca31a8372d0c353', certificates: [{}, {}] })) {\n  console.log(customCertificate);\n}\n```",
