    markdown:
      "## edit\n\n`client.keylessCertificates.edit(zone_id: string, keyless_certificate_id: string, enabled?: boolean, host?: string, name?: string, port?: number, tunnel?: { private_ip: string; vnet_id: string; }): { id: string; created_on: string; enabled: boolean; host: string; modified_on: string; name: string; permissions: string[]; port: number; status: 'active' | 'deleted'; tunnel?: tunnel; }`\n\n**patch** `/zones/{zone_id}/keyless_certificates/{keyless_certificate_id}`\n\nThis will update attributes of a Keyless SSL. Consists of one or more of the following:  host,name,port.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `zone_id: string`\n  Identifier.\n\n- `keyless_certificate_id: string`\n  Identifier.\n\n- `enabled?: boolean`\n  Whether or not the Keyless SSL is on or off.\n\n- `host?: string`\n  The keyless SSL name.\n\n- `name?: string`\n  The keyless SSL name.\n\n- `port?: number`\n  The keyless SSL port used to communicate between Cloudflare and the client's Keyless SSL server.\n\n- `tunnel?: { private_ip: string; vnet_id: string; }`\n  Configuration for using Keyless SSL through a Cloudflare Tunnel.\n  - `private_ip: string`\n    Private IP of the Key Server Host.\n  - `vnet_id: string`\n    Cloudflare Tunnel Virtual Network ID.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; created_on: string; enabled: boolean; host: string; modified_on: string; name: string; permissions: string[]; port: number; status: 'active' | 'deleted'; tunnel?: { private_ip: string; vnet_id: string; }; }`\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `created_on: string`\n  - `enabled: boolean`\n  - `host: string`\n  - `modified_on: string`\n  - `name: string`\n  - `permissions: string[]`\n  - `port: number`\n  - `status: 'active' | 'deleted'`\n  - `tunnel?: { private_ip: string; vnet_id: string; }`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Cloudflare from 'cloudflare';\n\nconst client = new Cloudflare();\n\nconst keylessCertificate = await client.keylessCertificates.edit('023e105f4ecef8ad9ca31a8372d0c353', { zone_id: '023e105f4ecef8ad9ca31a8372d0c353' });\n\nconsole.log(keylessCertificate);\n```",
