    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.diagnostics.traceroutes.create(account_id: string, targets: string[], colos?: string[], options?: { max_ttl?: number; packet_type?: 'icmp' | 'tcp' | 'udp' | 'gre' | 'gre+icmp'; packets_per_ttl?: number; port?: number; wait_time?: number; }): { colos?: object[]; target?: string; }`\n\n**post** `/accounts/{account_id}/diagnostics/traceroute`\n\nRun traceroutes from Cloudflare colos.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `account_id: string`\n  Identifier\n\n- `targets: string[]`\n\n- `colos?: string[]`\n  If no source colo names specified, all colos will be used. China colos are unavailable for traceroutes.\n\n- `options?: { max_ttl?: number; packet_type?: 'icmp' | 'tcp' | 'udp' | 'gre' | 'gre+icmp'; packets_per_ttl?: number; port?: number; wait_time?: number; }`\n  - `max_ttl?: number`\n    Max TTL.\n  - `packet_type?: 'icmp' | 'tcp' | 'udp' | 'gre' | 'gre+icmp'`\n    Type of packet sent.\n  - `packets_per_ttl?: number`\n    Number of packets sent at each TTL.\n  - `port?: number`\n    For UDP and TCP, specifies the destination port. For ICMP, specifies the initial ICMP sequence value. Default value 0 will choose the best value to use for each protocol.\n  - `wait_time?: number`\n    Set the time (in seconds) to wait for a response to a probe.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ colos?: { colo?: { city?: string; name?: string; }; error?: string; hops?: { nodes?: object[]; packets_lost?: number; packets_sent?: number; packets_ttl?: number; }[]; target_summary?: object; traceroute_time_ms?: number; }[]; target?: string; }`\n\n  - `colos?: { colo?: { city?: string; name?: string; }; error?: string; hops?: { nodes?: { asn?: string; ip?: string; labels?: string[]; max_rtt_ms?: number; mean_rtt_ms?: number; min_rtt_ms?: number; name?: string; packet_count?: number; std_dev_rtt_ms?: number; }[]; packets_lost?: number; packets_sent?: number; packets_ttl?: number; }[]; target_summary?: object; traceroute_time_ms?: number; }[]`\n  - `target?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Cloudflare from 'cloudflare';\n\nconst client = new Cloudflare();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const traceroute of client.diagnostics.traceroutes.create({ account_id: '023e105f4ecef8ad9ca31a8372d0c353', targets: ['203.0.113.1', 'cloudflare.com'] })) {\n  console.log(traceroute);\n}\n```",
