    markdown:
      "## edit\n\n`client.stream.edit(account_id: string, identifier: string, allowedOrigins?: string[], creator?: string, maxDurationSeconds?: number, meta?: object, publicDetails?: { channel_link?: string; logo?: string; share_link?: string; title?: string; }, requireSignedURLs?: boolean, scheduledDeletion?: string, thumbnailTimestampPct?: number, uid?: string, uploadExpiry?: string): { allowedOrigins?: allowed_origins[]; clippedFrom?: string; created?: string; creator?: string; duration?: number; input?: object; liveInput?: string; maxDurationSeconds?: number; maxSizeBytes?: number; meta?: object; modified?: string; playback?: object; preview?: string; publicDetails?: object; readyToStream?: boolean; readyToStreamAt?: string; requireSignedURLs?: boolean; scheduledDeletion?: string; size?: number; status?: object; thumbnail?: string; thumbnailTimestampPct?: number; uid?: string; uploaded?: string; uploadExpiry?: string; watermark?: watermark; }`\n\n**post** `/accounts/{account_id}/stream/{identifier}`\n\nEdit details for a single video.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `account_id: string`\n  The account identifier tag.\n\n- `identifier: string`\n  A Cloudflare-generated unique identifier for a media item.\n\n- `allowedOrigins?: string[]`\n  Lists the origins allowed to display the video. Enter allowed origin domains in an array and use `*` for wildcard subdomains. Empty arrays allow the video to be viewed on any origin.\n\n- `creator?: string`\n  A user-defined identifier for the media creator.\n\n- `maxDurationSeconds?: number`\n  The maximum duration in seconds for a video upload. Can be set for a video that is not yet uploaded to limit its duration. Uploads that exceed the specified duration will fail during processing. A value of `-1` means the value is unknown.\n\n- `meta?: object`\n  A user modifiable key-value store used to reference other systems of record for managing videos.\n\n- `publicDetails?: { channel_link?: string; logo?: string; share_link?: string; title?: string; }`\n  Public details for the video including title, share link, channel link, and logo.\n  - `channel_link?: string`\n  - `logo?: string`\n  - `share_link?: string`\n  - `title?: string`\n\n- `requireSignedURLs?: boolean`\n  Indicates whether the video can be a accessed using the UID. When set to `true`, a signed token must be generated with a signing key to view the video.\n\n- `scheduledDeletion?: string`\n  Indicates the date and time at which the video will be deleted. Omit the field to indicate no change, or include with a `null` value to remove an existing scheduled deletion. If specified, must be at least 30 days from upload time.\n\n- `thumbnailTimestampPct?: number`\n  The timestamp for a thumbnail image calculated as a percentage value of the video's duration. To convert from a second-wise timestamp to a percentage, divide the desired timestamp by the total duration of the video.  If this value is not set, the default thumbnail image is taken from 0s of the video.\n\n- `uid?: string`\n  The unique identifier for the video. Can be used to verify the video being updated.\n\n- `uploadExpiry?: string`\n  The date and time when the video upload URL is no longer valid for direct user uploads.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ allowedOrigins?: string[]; clippedFrom?: string; created?: string; creator?: string; duration?: number; input?: { height?: number; width?: number; }; liveInput?: string; maxDurationSeconds?: number; maxSizeBytes?: number; meta?: object; modified?: string; playback?: { dash?: string; hls?: string; }; preview?: string; publicDetails?: { channel_link?: string; logo?: string; media_id?: number; share_link?: string; title?: string; }; readyToStream?: boolean; readyToStreamAt?: string; requireSignedURLs?: boolean; scheduledDeletion?: string; size?: number; status?: { errorReasonCode?: string; errorReasonText?: string; pctComplete?: string; state?: 'pendingupload' | 'downloading' | 'queued' | 'inprogress' | 'ready' | 'error' | 'live-inprogress'; }; thumbnail?: string; thumbnailTimestampPct?: number; uid?: string; uploaded?: string; uploadExpiry?: string; watermark?: { created?: string; downloadedFrom?: string; height?: number; name?: string; opacity?: number; padding?: number; position?: string; scale?: number; size?: number; uid?: string; width?: number; }; }`\n\n  - `allowedOrigins?: string[]`\n  - `clippedFrom?: string`\n  - `created?: string`\n  - `creator?: string`\n  - `duration?: number`\n  - `input?: { height?: number; width?: number; }`\n  - `liveInput?: string`\n  - `maxDurationSeconds?: number`\n  - `maxSizeBytes?: number`\n  - `meta?: object`\n  - `modified?: string`\n  - `playback?: { dash?: string; hls?: string; }`\n  - `preview?: string`\n  - `publicDetails?: { channel_link?: string; logo?: string; media_id?: number; share_link?: string; title?: string; }`\n  - `readyToStream?: boolean`\n  - `readyToStreamAt?: string`\n  - `requireSignedURLs?: boolean`\n  - `scheduledDeletion?: string`\n  - `size?: number`\n  - `status?: { errorReasonCode?: string; errorReasonText?: string; pctComplete?: string; state?: 'pendingupload' | 'downloading' | 'queued' | 'inprogress' | 'ready' | 'error' | 'live-inprogress'; }`\n  - `thumbnail?: string`\n  - `thumbnailTimestampPct?: number`\n  - `uid?: string`\n  - `uploaded?: string`\n  - `uploadExpiry?: string`\n  - `watermark?: { created?: string; downloadedFrom?: string; height?: number; name?: string; opacity?: number; padding?: number; position?: string; scale?: number; size?: number; uid?: string; width?: number; }`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Cloudflare from 'cloudflare';\n\nconst client = new Cloudflare();\n\nconst video = await client.stream.edit('ea95132c15732412d22c1476fa83f27a', { account_id: '023e105f4ecef8ad9ca31a8372d0c353' });\n\nconsole.log(video);\n```",
