    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.zeroTrust.networks.subnets.list(account_id: string, address_family?: 'v4' | 'v6', comment?: string, existed_at?: string, is_default_network?: boolean, is_deleted?: boolean, name?: string, network?: string, page?: number, per_page?: number, sort_order?: 'asc' | 'desc', subnet_types?: 'cloudflare_source' | 'warp'): { id?: string; comment?: string; created_at?: string; deleted_at?: string; is_default_network?: boolean; name?: string; network?: string; subnet_type?: 'cloudflare_source' | 'warp'; }`\n\n**get** `/accounts/{account_id}/zerotrust/subnets`\n\nLists and filters subnets in an account.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `account_id: string`\n  Cloudflare account ID\n\n- `address_family?: 'v4' | 'v6'`\n  If set, only include subnets in the given address family - `v4` or `v6`\n\n- `comment?: string`\n  If set, only list subnets with the given comment.\n\n- `existed_at?: string`\n  If provided, include only resources that were created (and not deleted) before this time. URL encoded.\n\n- `is_default_network?: boolean`\n  If `true`, only include default subnets. If `false`, exclude default subnets subnets. If not set, all subnets will be included.\n\n- `is_deleted?: boolean`\n  If `true`, only include deleted subnets. If `false`, exclude deleted subnets. If not set, all subnets will be included.\n\n- `name?: string`\n  If set, only list subnets with the given name\n\n- `network?: string`\n  If set, only list the subnet whose network exactly matches the given CIDR.\n\n- `page?: number`\n  Page number of paginated results.\n\n- `per_page?: number`\n  Number of results to display.\n\n- `sort_order?: 'asc' | 'desc'`\n  Sort order of the results. `asc` means oldest to newest, `desc` means newest to oldest. If not set, they will not be in any particular order.\n\n- `subnet_types?: 'cloudflare_source' | 'warp'`\n  If set, the types of subnets to include, separated by comma.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id?: string; comment?: string; created_at?: string; deleted_at?: string; is_default_network?: boolean; name?: string; network?: string; subnet_type?: 'cloudflare_source' | 'warp'; }`\n\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `comment?: string`\n  - `created_at?: string`\n  - `deleted_at?: string`\n  - `is_default_network?: boolean`\n  - `name?: string`\n  - `network?: string`\n  - `subnet_type?: 'cloudflare_source' | 'warp'`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Cloudflare from 'cloudflare';\n\nconst client = new Cloudflare();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const subnet of client.zeroTrust.networks.subnets.list({ account_id: '699d98642c564d2e855e9661899b7252' })) {\n  console.log(subnet);\n}\n```",
